  "conclusions": [
    "For gfx12.1, device initialization selects the built-in cwsr_trap_gfx12_1_0_hex array. The reviewed selection/copy path does not request a separate firmware blob; changing a filesystem firmware image is not an activation path for this table.",
    "CWSR process initialization reserves a GPU TBA/TMA buffer, copies the device table to it, and makes qpd.tba_addr the reserved CWSR base. The user trap-registration ioctl writes only second-level TBA/TMA slots while cwsr_kaddr exists.",
    "Trap registration before process-VM initialization cannot retain an overriding first-level address because subsequent CWSR initialization assigns tba_addr unconditionally. CWSR initialization precedes normal VM use.",
    "The selected CWSR allocation requests executable memory without KFD_IOC_ALLOC_MEM_FLAGS_WRITABLE. The reviewed page-table flag function consequently maps this buffer readable and executable, without the GPU write flag; ordinary GPU stores are not a supported patch route.",
    "The old /dev/kfd reserved-memory mmap case is explicitly rejected with EINVAL. Only doorbell and MMIO mapping cases are accepted by this dispatcher; they do not select the CWSR buffer.",
    "The CWSR helper passes NULL for the allocation mmap-offset result and creates no public KFD allocation-IDR handle. The GEM handle is created in the driver-owned KFD client file, not returned as a userspace GEM handle. Ordinary KFD allocation/export/checkpoint handling operates on alloc_idr objects; this CWSR allocation is not added there.",
